{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Like a House on Fire", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Breaking the News", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 18, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in written and spoken situations and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": " The Future Continuous and Future Perfect Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Future Continuous tense </span> to talk about something happening at a particular time in the future. <br> When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous</span>, the action will have started before that moment, but it will not have finished at that moment. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\"> will be working</span> at 4 p.m. tomorrow. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The person will start work at some point in the future and be working at 4 p.m. It is not clear when the person will stop working. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the<span class=\"strong\"> Future Perfect tense</span> to talk about an action in the future that happens before another action in the future (often in present tense).  <br> When you use the <span class=\"strong\"> Future Perfect</span>, you can sometimes think of the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect tense </span> like the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect tense</span>, but instead of your viewpoint being in the present, it is in the future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You can call me at work at 8 a.m. I <span class=\"strong\">will have arrived</span> at the office by 8 a.m.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">The train will leave the station at 9 a.m. You will arrive at the station at 9:15 a.m. When you arrive, the train <span class=\"strong\">will have left</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Look at the chart for the structure of the <span class=\"strong\">Future Continuous </span>and <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect </span> tenses:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Name\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" will (not) + be + v-ing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">ll be working </span> all week.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" will + have + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Vanessa <span class=\\\"strong\\\">will have worked </span> on this a lot by that time.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You, me and Vanessa will have gone to a million activities by the time this year ends, so what if I miss one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sorry I have to break this news to you, but I forgot Andrew and I will be playing softball on Sunday and then we will be attending a party.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That is nice to say, but by Sunday, I will not have finished this thing. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Vanessa thinks I will have finished everything by Sunday, but I won't and to be honest, I don't want to go axe throwing.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " The Future", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use four different tenses to talk about the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are not decided or when you make a decision at the moment of speaking for the future, you use the modal <span class=\"italic\">will.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you ask about intentions, you use <span class=\"italic\">be going to.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about things that are arranged, on the agenda or booked for the future, you use the Present Continuous tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you talk about schedules, you use the Simple Present. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Will/won't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">You won't be able to make the axe-throwing event?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Be going to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm going to be working on a press release.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Are you going axe throwing?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I work this weekend, Saturday and Sunday.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I work this weekend, Saturday and Sunday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Yes, I will go.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll call you later.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "overloaded", "type": "name"}, {"content": "having more work than you can do", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm overloaded. I'll be working all week.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob06aud01 ", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when asking for reasons about something.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "inquisitive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "eager to know more about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Why are you so inquisitive about what I'm doing?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "have a good time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "enjoy oneself", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We always have a good time with you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "softball", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a game similar to baseball,  played on a smaller field with a larger ball", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I forgot Andrew and I will be playing softball on Sunday. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "not my bag", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to express that something is not your preference", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Dancing is just not my bag.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le18ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "In pairs, brainstorm all the different excuses that people use.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create six situations that you don't want to do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Give another pair of students the situations that you and your partner have created.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The pairs must think up some good excuses not to do the situation and role play the dialogue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use verbs for future action to describe what you will be doing in the future and give reasons as to why you can't do them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Vote for the best one.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm different excuses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about future ideas to convey excuses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I role play the situations.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn9le18ob06re2img01.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob06re2img01.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Peter</span>: Hello?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Peter. It's Sally. How are you doing?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Peter</span>: Good, but I'm overloaded. I'll be working all week.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: I heard. You won't be able to make the axe-throwing event?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Peter</span>: No. I work this weekend, Saturday and Sunday. Are you going?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Yes, I will go.<br />"}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob06re2img02.jpg", "time": "23000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: What are you going to be working on? <br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Peter</span>: I'm going to be working on a press release. Why so inquisitive?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: We always have a good time with you and I was wondering if there is there anything I could do to help out?<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Peter</span>: Thank you Sally. That is nice to say, but by Sunday, I will not have finished this thing. I know Vanessa thinks I will have finished everything by Sunday, but I won't and to be honest, I don't want to go axe throwing.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Why not? Vanessa will have worked on this a lot by the time Sunday rolls around.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Peter</span>: Because I'd rather do something else. I'm sorry I said yes. It's just not my bag.<br />"}, {"image": "engenn9le18ob06re2img05.jpg", "time": "58500", "id": 3, "text": "<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Vanessa really would like you to be there. She is counting on you.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Peter</span>: You, me and Vanessa will have gone to a million activities by the time this year ends, so what if I miss one. Listen. I got to get back. I'll call you later.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Bye.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Robert</span>: Hi. Sally. It's Robert. Listen Sally. Sorry I have to break this news to you, but I forgot Andrew and I will be playing softball on Sunday and then we will be attending a party. So we can't make it. Sorry. Hope you find someone.<br />\n<span class= \"strong\"> Sally</span>: Oh boy.<br />"}], "audiosrc": "engenn9le18ob06re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn9le18ob06re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can talk about emotions, personal qualities and behavior.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about future action.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what I will be doing or what I will have done.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What are some common excuses people give when they don't want to do something or go somewhere?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Have you ever used any of these excuses? Which ones?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "